body:
> It seems clipboard provider is broken.

Both providers share the same stderr callback now.  That was the purpose of the commit, to provide a common way for the providers to collect stderr.

> You can get the error by the text yank.

Unfortunately, just using that config and performing a yank doesn't reproduce the issue for me.

What we need is a reliable way to reproduce the issue so we can understand why the callback is being called without a self dictionary.

If someone can reproduce this and doesn't mind investigating the problem from a core dump, then this patch should make nvim crash when we hit the problem:

```diff
diff --git a/src/nvim/eval.c b/src/nvim/eval.c
index 78c8dd02d..a4267589e 100644
--- a/src/nvim/eval.c
+++ b/src/nvim/eval.c
@@ -6387,6 +6387,7 @@ call_func(
         } else if (!fp->uf_varargs && argcount > fp->uf_args.ga_len) {
           error = ERROR_TOOMANY;
         } else if ((fp->uf_flags & FC_DICT) && selfdict == NULL) {
+          abort();
           error = ERROR_DICT;
         } else {
           // Call the user function.
```
